<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Tree Context Menus</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>Tree context menus appear when user right clicks on a tree item. There are mainly three types of commands in this menu:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Common%20and%20Selection%20Commands">Common and Selection commands</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Visualisation_Commands">Visualisation commands</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Specific_Commands_for_Datuming">Specific commands for datuming</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Transformations">Specific commands for transformations</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Transformations1">Specific commands for Current CS</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Specific_commands_for_View_Positions">Specific commands for view positions</a></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2><a name="Common and Selection Commands"></a>Common and Selection Commands</h2>
<p class="whs4"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Commands selected for an item of higher level will affect to all sub-items that are derived from it. For example, if you choose</font></span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path">Rendering &gt; Wireframe</span></i> <span lang="EN-US">for Scans group, all scan data entities will be displayed in</span> <span class="Mode">wireframe</span> <span lang="EN-US">mode. If you want to display as polygons a particular scan data entity, then right-click on this entity and select</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path">Rendering &gt; Wireframe</span></i> <span lang="EN-US">from its context menu.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">You can call context menu for several entities and groups at once. They must be marked first. There are two ways of marking entities/groups:</font></span></p>
<ol start="1" class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-US">Hold down</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">key and click on different entities/groups to mark them.</span></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP223638983" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="Images/tree_context.gif" width="189px" height="271px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<ol start="2" class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-US">Hold down</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">key and click on two entities/groups. All items between them will be marked.</span></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP223708864" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="whs7"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;"><img src="Images/tree_context_2.gif" width="198px" height="290px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></font></span></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">If you marked more than one entity/group the common context menu will appear. It contains only select/unselect, hide/show, and delete commands. Tree context menus for single entity/group vary depending on the data type.</font></span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P8"><span lang="EN-US">Note that marking (highlighting) and selecting entities are two different actions. Mark single or multiple items to invoke a particular or common context menu. Use selection to apply processing commands to specific entities or particular areas from entities.</span></p>
<p class="Warning" id="p12"><span lang="EN-GB">Cut</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB">Copy</span><span lang="EN-GB">, and</span> <span lang="EN-GB">Paste</span> <span lang="EN-GB">(for groups only) commands from the tree context menus are per entity/group.&#160;</span></p>
<p class="ExampleCode" id="p12"><span lang="EN-GB">For example:<br>
<br>
1. If one scan data entity and one mesh entity are selected and</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Cut</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is called from the mesh entity context menu then only the mesh entity will be cut to the clipboard. If</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b><a href="../References/cut.htm">Edit &gt; Cut</a></b></i></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is selected or</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + X</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">shortcut is used then both entities will be cut to the clipboard.<br>
<br>
2. If one scan data entity and one mesh entity are selected and</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Copy</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is called from the mesh entity context menu then only the mesh entity will be copied in the clipboard. If</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b><a href="../References/copy.htm">Edit &gt; Copy</a></b></i></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is selected or</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + C</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">shortcut is used then both entities will be copied in the clipboard.<br>
<br>
3. If one scan data entity and one mesh entity are copied in the clipboard and</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Paste</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is called from the Meshes group then only the mesh entity will be pasted. If</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b><a href="../References/Paste_as_New_Entity.htm">Edit &gt; Paste as New Entity</a></b></i></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is selected or</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + V</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">shortcut is used then both entities will be pasted into their corresponding groups.</span></p>
<h3><span lang="EN-US">Common Context Menu</span></h3>
<p><span lang="EN-US">I</span>f you mark more than one entity/group the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>common context menu</b></span> only will appear.</p>
